{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>He crouched, he lay down, etc.</b> The meaning is: even at the time when he crouched — meaning he does not gird weapons and does not stand for battle but rather crouches and sits at ease — and not this alone, but even when he lay down, so that he feels nothing of those coming upon him, even so he is not afraid, for who is this who would approach him to rouse him? And its saying <b>and as a lion</b> — he doubled the gradations corresponding to two classes within Israel, one above the other as we wrote above, namely the righteous and the intermediate." "<b>Those who bless you are blessed, etc.</b> He said <b>those who bless you</b> in plural form and <b>blessed</b> in singular — he did not wish to bless except one, and he intended himself, and his eye was evil toward the rest of those who bless. And he said <b>those who curse you are cursed</b> — he intended to say that not all who curse him are cursed, and he came to diminish himself from the cursing. Or perhaps his intention was for evil along these lines: those who bless you — may their words be fulfilled and you shall be blessed; and those who curse you — may their words be fulfilled and you shall be, etc. — and the wicked one schemed by this in order to establish it if he curses them afterward. Therefore he placed the statement of <b>blessed</b> before <b>cursed</b>, to place them under a curse, Heaven forbid. But HaShem repaid him in kind, and the curse was fulfilled upon him, and he was cursed in this world and in the World to Come, as they said, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 105a): Balaam has no share in the World to Come."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:47.149778005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}